    <content>
        <description>
            <levelledPara>
                <para>The Stratos avionics system is centred on a flight controller running
                    ArduPilot open-source autopilot firmware. The flight controller processes sensor
                    data and control inputs at 400 Hz, computing motor speed corrections to maintain
                    the commanded flight path.</para>
            </levelledPara>
            <levelledPara>
                <para>Attitude and heading reference is provided by a nine-axis inertial measurement
                    unit (IMU) that combines a three-axis accelerometer, three-axis gyroscope, and
                    three-axis magnetometer. GPS position and velocity are provided by a
                    dual-frequency GNSS receiver with an accuracy of ±1.5 m horizontal under
                    open-sky conditions.</para>
            </levelledPara>
            <levelledPara>
                <para>The GCS communications link operates on the 2.4 GHz ISM band using
                    frequency-hopping spread spectrum to minimise interference and interception.
                    Link range is 5 km under line-of-sight conditions. If the link is lost, the
                    flight controller automatically executes a return-to-home sequence.</para>
            </levelledPara>
        </description>
